# CI: fix the flaky Real verify phrase check (SIGPIPE under pipefail).
#
# THE FAILURE
# -----------
# Run 44546772543 (SHA 02d0b4a), 2026-11-19, failed its Real verify
# step with:
#
#     ##[error]gustale.com/dishes/bakso/ does not contain 'Indonesian
#     meatball' (live data not on the page)
#     ##[error]Real verify FAILED for run 44546772543 at SHA 02d0b4a
#
# It was NOT a content bug. The deployed artifact and the live page
# both contained the phrase three times:
#
#     $ md5sum  (bakso HTML from the 02d0b4a image)
#     6baedb2edaeb2ab59d9377fe7f6c2216   52250 bytes
#     $ grep -c "Indonesian meatball" ...
#     3
#
# The 02d0b4a and 663f05b artifacts are byte-identical (same size, same
# MD5), so no content change was involved. The next deploy, 663f05b
# (run 44588963284), passed the same check.
#
# THE CAUSE
# ---------
# The step runs under `set -euo pipefail` (ci.yml line 2125). The check
# was:
#
#     if [ -n "${PAGE:-}" ] && echo "$PAGE" | grep -qF "$PHRASE"; then
#
# `grep -q` exits the moment it finds the match. `echo` is still
# writing the 52 KB body, gets SIGPIPE, and dies with 141. With
# `pipefail`, the PIPELINE's status is then 141 -- non-zero -- so the
# `if` takes the ELSE branch and reports the phrase as missing, even
# though grep matched it and the page contains it.
#
# It is a RACE, not a deterministic fault, which is why it hit one
# deploy and not the next.
#
# MEASURED ON THE DEPLOY HOST (62.72.7.218), 2026-11-20
# -------------------------------------------------------
# The OLD form, 600 iterations per body size:
#
#     CURRENT (echo | grep -q) full       : fails=2/600  (rc=141 in 2)
#     CURRENT (echo | grep -q) truncated  : fails=4/600  (rc=141 in 4)
#     CURRENT (echo | grep -q) small      : fails=3/600  (rc=141 in 3)
#
# 9 false failures in 1800 iterations, EVERY one of them rc=141.
#
# The NEW form, same host, same iteration count:
#
#     FIXED (case pattern)      full       : fails=0/600
#     FIXED (case pattern)      truncated  : fails=0/600
#     FIXED (case pattern)      small      : fails=0/600
#
# THE FIX
# -------
# The bash `case`/parameter-expansion form has NO pipeline and NO
# SIGPIPE, so it cannot race:
#
#     if [ -n "${PAGE:-}" ] && [[ "$PAGE" == *"$PHRASE"* ]]; then
#
# The check still fails for a genuinely wrong page -- a missing phrase
# is still a missing phrase. It only removes the false negative.
#
# HOW TO APPLY IT
# ---------------
# The GitHub App (`gustale-bot`) has NO `workflows` scope, so a workflow
# change cannot be pushed. Apply this patch:
#
#     git checkout main && git pull
#     git apply docs/ci-real-verify-sigpipe-fix.patch
#     git commit -m "ci: fix the flaky Real verify phrase check"
#     git push
#
# VERIFICATION
# ------------
#     python3 -c "import yaml,sys; yaml.safe_load(open('.github/workflows/ci.yml'))"
#
# The patched `ci.yml` parses, `bash -n` is clean on the patched
# snippet, and the patched check passes against the live page:
#
#     gustale.com/dishes/bakso/ contains 'Indonesian meatball'  OK
#
diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 573c315..416356b 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -2263,13 +2263,31 @@ jobs:
               echo "--- Check 3: live page phrase ---"
               PHRASE="Indonesian meatball"  # from the bakso longDescription
               PAGE=$(curl -fsS --max-time 10 "https://gustale.com/dishes/bakso/" 2>&1) || {
                 echo "::error::curl https://gustale.com/dishes/bakso/ failed"
                 FAILED=1
               }
-              if [ -n "${PAGE:-}" ] && echo "$PAGE" | grep -qF "$PHRASE"; then
+              # NOT `echo "$PAGE" | grep -qF "$PHRASE"`.
+              #
+              # This step runs under `set -euo pipefail`. `grep -q` exits
+              # the moment it matches, so `echo` is killed by SIGPIPE
+              # (141) while it is still writing the 52 KB body. With
+              # pipefail the PIPELINE's status is then 141 -- non-zero --
+              # and the `if` takes the else branch, reporting the phrase
+              # as MISSING even though grep matched it and the page
+              # contains it.
+              #
+              # That is exactly what happened on run 44546772543
+              # (SHA 02d0b4a) on 2026-11-19: the deployed artifact and
+              # the live page both contained the phrase three times,
+              # and the check still failed. The bash `case` form below
+              # has no pipeline and no SIGPIPE, so it cannot race:
+              # measured on the deploy host, the old form failed
+              # 9 times in 1800 iterations (every one rc=141) and this
+              # form failed 0 times in 1800.
+              if [ -n "${PAGE:-}" ] && [[ "$PAGE" == *"$PHRASE"* ]]; then
                 echo "  gustale.com/dishes/bakso/ contains '$PHRASE'  OK"
               else
                 echo "::error::gustale.com/dishes/bakso/ does not contain '$PHRASE' (live data not on the page)"
                 FAILED=1
               fi
 
